MEDICAL REFORMS OF THE FIFTH HOKAGE
Tsunade Senju, Godaime Hokage — Office Directive

As the world's foremost medical-nin and a granddaughter of the First
Hokage, the Godaime instituted sweeping reforms to shinobi medicine:

1. Every four-person squad deployed on B-rank or higher missions shall
   include at least one field-trained medical-nin.
2. Expansion of the Medical Corps and standardization of the Mystical
   Palm healing technique in Academy senior curriculum.
3. Establishment of a poison-and-antidote research section following
   lessons from prior campaigns.
4. Mandatory chakra-reserve and fitness assessment before high-rank
   deployment (see medical records).

The Godaime's guiding principle: a shinobi's life is not to be spent
carelessly. These reforms materially reduced field mortality. By order
of Tsunade, Fifth Hokage.
